1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,374
Every family has a beginning. Ours
begins at the old walls of Harar.

2
00:00:07,074 --> 00:00:14,292
My great-grandparents came here from far
away, carrying little more than a skill.

3
00:00:14,991 --> 00:00:21,191
My great-grandfather was a tailor on
Makina Girgir, the street of sewing

4
00:00:21,191 --> 00:00:21,977
machines.

5
00:00:22,678 --> 00:00:27,446
My grandmother kept a small stall by the
street. The stitches became trade, and

6
00:00:27,446 --> 00:00:29,035
the trade became a living.

7
00:00:29,734 --> 00:00:34,247
What she earned, she saved, for the ones
who would come after her.

8
00:00:35,234 --> 00:00:42,089
My mother helped her at the stall by
day, and carried her schoolbooks with

9
00:00:42,089 --> 00:00:42,465
her.

10
00:00:43,165 --> 00:00:47,657
At night, when she was tired, she
studied anyway.

11
00:00:49,165 --> 00:00:52,024
And one day, she graduated.

12
00:00:55,165 --> 00:01:00,033
Then she worked long hours in a
government office, and gave everything

13
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:02,149
she had so that I could learn.

14
00:01:02,849 --> 00:01:09,092
I graduated in software engineering with
honours, won a scholarship for my

15
00:01:09,092 --> 00:01:14,992
master's, and today I am an AI engineer,
with comforts they never had.

16
00:01:15,692 --> 00:01:22,265
Nothing I have is mine alone. It is the
work of everyone who came before me. Now

17
00:01:22,265 --> 00:01:25,676
it is my turn to take us a little
further.

